[32m+ ## Monthly Dataset Update[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ At the start of a new month, place the latest NESO demand CSV in `Downloads` using one of these names:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `demanddata_YYYY.csv`[m
[32m+ - `demanddataupdate_YYYY.csv`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ Then run:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```powershell[m
[32m+ python uk_training_data_prep\run_monthly_dataset_update.py[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ This runs:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - local UK holiday/economic feature refresh[m
[32m+ - combined weather feature rebuild[m
[32m+ - hourly demand rebuild[m
[32m+ - master training dataset rebuild[m
[32m+ - forecast feature dataset rebuild[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The local feature refresh reads the existing source files in `data/external/uk_features` and regenerates the project-ready `2010_onwards` files. The GitHub release synchronizer is kept separately for later online updates.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The final master file is:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `data/processed/master_training_data.csv`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The prediction input file is:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `data/processed/forecast_feature_data.csv`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ `master_training_data.csv` contains historical rows with `demand_mw` for training. `forecast_feature_data.csv` contains future weather timestamps joined with calendar/holiday and economic features for inference.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ## Hourly Load Data[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ To rebuild only the hourly UK load file, run:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```powershell[m
[32m+ python uk_training_data_prep\build_hourly_load_data.py[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ This reads NESO demand files from:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `data/raw/neso/`[m
[32m+ - your user `Downloads` folder, or the folder set in `DEMAND_INPUT_FOLDER`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ Outputs:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `data/uk_load_hourly.csv`[m
[32m+ - `data/uk_load_2010_YYYY_MM_DD_hourly.csv`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The load builder caps output at the current UTC hour. This prevents future zero rows from NESO update files being written into `uk_load_hourly.csv`. Old timestamped `uk_load_2010_*_hourly.csv` files are deleted before the newest one is created.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ To refresh only the local holiday/economic feature copies and rebuild the master dataset from the browser, use:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `Refresh Local Features + Rebuild Master`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ By default the monthly runner does not call the live weather API. If you want the monthly update to fetch fresh rolling weather as well, set this in `uk_training_data_prep/run_monthly_dataset_update.py`:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```python[m
[32m+ RUN_WEATHER_API_UPDATE = True[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ## Yearly Rolling Window[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ `build_master_training_data.py` applies a yearly rolling training window:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```python[m
[32m+ ENABLE_YEARLY_ROLLING_WINDOW = True[m
[32m+ ROLLING_WINDOW_YEARS_BEFORE_CURRENT_YEAR = 16[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ That means:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - during 2026, the master dataset starts at `2010-01-01`[m
[32m+ - on `2027-01-01`, it starts at `2011-01-01`[m
[32m+ - on `2028-01-01`, it starts at `2012-01-01`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ This keeps the dataset current without growing forever.[m
